# NO SECRETS HERE. Token lives in ~/.config/tts-bot/token (chmod 600), see README.
# First-boot SEED only: used once to populate config.json when it does not exist yet.
# After that the web UI / config.json is the source of truth and this value is ignored.
# Right-click the text channel in Discord (Developer Mode on) -> Copy Channel ID
TTS_CHANNEL_ID=
COMMAND_PREFIX=!
PIPER_MODEL_PATH=models/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx
PIPER_CONFIG_PATH=models/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx.json
# Folder scanned for voices in the GUI's Voice tab (default: the folder of PIPER_MODEL_PATH).
# PIPER_MODEL_PATH stays the fallback default; the voice chosen in the GUI is saved in config.json.
# PIPER_MODELS_DIR=models
MAX_CHARS=300
MAX_QUEUE=20
STATE_FILE=state.json
# Optional override of token file location
# DISCORD_TOKEN_FILE=~/.config/tts-bot/token
# Runtime config (channel selection) written by the web UI
# CONFIG_FILE=state/config.json   (default: next to STATE_FILE)
# Web UI users (scrypt hashes) for login (default: users.json next to CONFIG_FILE). Login is REQUIRED and fails
# closed: a missing/empty/invalid file means nobody can sign in. Create users with
#   python webui.py --users-file users.json add-user NAME --admin
# USERS_FILE=users.json
# DEV ONLY: exactly "off" (any case) disables the web UI login entirely and logs a warning. Never set this on a
# shared host or in production; any value other than "off" keeps login required.
# WEBUI_AUTH=off
# Web UI network settings. Binds loopback + auto-detected Tailscale addresses.
# WEBUI_PORT=8765
# Explicit bind list (loopback / Tailscale addresses only; anything else disables the GUI). Include 127.0.0.1;
# in explicit mode only these addresses are retried (auto mode re-detects Tailscale every 15 s):
# WEBUI_HOSTS=127.0.0.1,100.64.0.1
# Extra Host names to answer to (MagicDNS name, later your domain); hostnames only, no wildcards:
# WEBUI_ALLOWED_HOSTS=your-machine.tailnet-name.ts.net
